  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Total number of five-digit numbers are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mfenced><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Case I :&nbsp;Choosing&nbsp;two non-zero digits i.e. in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p>So, number of five-digit numbers containing both digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Case II :&nbsp;Choose one non-zero and&nbsp;one zero as digit i.e. in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p>So, number of five-digit numbers containing one non-zero and one zero both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>So, favourable number of ways&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mfenced><mn>30</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mn>15</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1080</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>135</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1215</mn></math></p><p>Thus, required probability&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1215</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>135</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p>",
